cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AI Adoption, Labour Productivity, and Carbon Emissions —
  agent-based simulation code
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the thesis it
  supports.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-19"
authors:
  - family-names: Ben Khadher
    given-names: Amir
    affiliation: University of Mannheim
abstract: >-
  Agent-based simulation of AI adoption in a heterogeneous
  population of firms, and of its net effect on operational
  carbon emissions. Adoption spreads through a
  sector-specific innovation-and-imitation hazard; each
  agent's net effect sets an AI-induced fall in carbon
  intensity against the emissions of the electricity AI
  consumes, priced at its national grid. The code reproduces
  every table and figure of Chapters 4 to 6 of the
  supporting bachelor thesis, including the break-even
  analysis that locates the output-scale response at which
  the net effect changes sign.
keywords:
  - agent-based model
  - artificial intelligence
  - carbon emissions
  - rebound effect
  - labour productivity
  - environmental economics
  - reproducible research
repository-code: https://github.com/Amir-stu/ai-adoption-emissions-abm
license: MIT
